@implements IDisposable
@* One named area of a site's page (F117, ADR 0106): a section that must carry an id, a topic over its content, and the
   classes a site adds for its look. The id is what the guide's ShowPage names and the section index links, so a page
   built of bands has every area named by construction, and the band puts itself on the frame's list as it draws
   (F118). The band draws no style of its own: .band and .topic are the site's, so each site keeps its look. Its body
   lays out as if it weren't there; on a page of slides, when it holds more than a screen, the frame's module pages it
   sideways and shows the pager beside it (F118). *@
<section id="@Id" class="@Classes" data-whole="@Whole">
    <div class="band-body">
        @* A mark over the topic (F169.3), drawing only. *@
        @if (Mark is not null)
        {
            <div class="band-mark" aria-hidden="true">@Mark</div>
        }
        @if (Topic is not null)
        {
            <span class="topic">@Topic</span>
        }
        @* The band hands itself down, so a title in it knows whether it heads the page (FX125). *@
        <CascadingValue Value="this" IsFixed="true">
            @* A site configures the band's head (ADR 0125): its heading, its summary and a note after it. *@
            @if (Title is not null)
            {
                <BandTitle Class="chrome reveal">@Title</BandTitle>
            }
            @if (Summary is not null)
            {
                <p class="summary reveal">@Markdown.Inline(Summary)</p>
            }
            @ChildContent
            @if (Note is not null)
            {
                <p class="band-note">@Markdown.Inline(Note)</p>
            }
        </CascadingValue>
    </div>
    <div class="band-pager" hidden>
        <button type="button" class="band-page" data-step="-1" aria-label="Previous page">‹</button>
        <span class="band-pages" aria-live="polite"></span>
        <button type="button" class="band-page" data-step="1" aria-label="Next page">›</button>
    </div>
</section>
